      en: ["The ginnery was officially inaugurated in 1947 as part of the colonial Zande Scheme.", "It is located in Western Equatoria State, near the border with the Democratic Republic of Congo.", "The site once processed cotton for textiles and extracted oil from cotton seeds for soap.", "The Zande Scheme was initiated by British official James Wyld to foster rural development.", "During the 1950s, Nzara was a major industrial employer with over 1,000 workers.", "Efforts are currently underway to re-engage local farmers in cotton farming to supply the mill."],
